+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: each immediate subdirectory of the workspace root whose newest
+file is more than the threshold number of days old. A workspace with no files is aged by its own
+modification time. Symlinks in the root are never followed or removed.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [--root DIR] [--days N] [--dry-run]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` (relative to the current directory) | Directory containing the workspaces |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Remove workspaces older than N whole days |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | Print `would remove ...` lines and delete nothing |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --dry-run                      # preview with the defaults
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/work --days 3   # a worker with a different layout
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` on success, `64` for a usage error (bad option or `--days`, or a root of `/`),
+`66` if the root is not a directory.
